{#
  The numbered notes at the foot of a piece.

  The reading experience is not here. A marker in the prose opens its note under
  the paragraph that cited it, in _partials/prose.twig, so the reader never
  leaves the line they are on. This list is the reference: it is what a printed
  or saved page needs, and what someone scanning the citations wants to see
  together.

  Four sources, one list.

    [mfn]...[/mfn]   the WordPress Modern Footnotes shortcode from the previous
                     site, read straight out of the prose and numbered in
                     document order from 1. Reading it here means a record is
                     right before the conversion script has been run on it and
                     identical afterwards.
    footnotes        the table field, once the conversion has written it.
    footnotesOn      the notes were published on another record. Nothing is
                     listed; the piece says where they are.
    neither          orphan. The markers are the author's and the notes they
                     refer to did not survive. Said once, plainly.

  The fields are read through the layout, because entry.footnotes is "defined"
  on a type that has no such field and throws the moment it is read.

  Params:
    entry   the record
#}
{%- set handles = [] -%}
{%- for f in entry.fieldLayout.customFields -%}{%- set handles = handles|merge([f.handle]) -%}{%- endfor -%}

{%- set rows = 'footnotes' in handles ? (entry.footnotes ?? []) : [] -%}
{%- set notesOn = 'footnotesOn' in handles ? (entry.footnotesOn.one() ?? null) : null -%}

{#- The prose, for both the shortcode notes and the orphan test. Every PlainText
    field, in layout order, which is the order prose.twig sees them in. Reading
    a named three found nothing on records that plainly carry markers. -#}
{%- set prose = '' -%}
{%- for f in entry.fieldLayout.customFields -%}
  {%- if f.className == 'craft\\fields\\PlainText' or className(f) == 'craft\\fields\\PlainText' -%}
    {%- set prose = prose ~ "\n" ~ attribute(entry, f.handle) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{#- Shortcode notes, in document order. Only where the table is empty: once the
    conversion has run, the rows are the authority and the body holds [N]. -#}
{%- set notes = [] -%}
{%- if rows|length -%}
  {%- for r in rows -%}
    {%- set notes = notes|merge([{ n: (r.number ?? '')|trim ?: loop.index, t: (r.note ?? '')|trim }]) -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- elseif prose|lower|split('[mfn')|length > 1 -%}
  {%- for part in prose|split('[mfn')|slice(1) -%}
    {%- set afterOpen = part|split(']')|length > 1 ? part|slice(part|split(']')|first|length + 1) : '' -%}
    {%- if afterOpen and afterOpen|split('[/mfn]')|length > 1 -%}
      {%- set notes = notes|merge([{ n: notes|length + 1, t: afterOpen|split('[/mfn]')|first|trim }]) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- set hasMarker = prose matches '/(?<![A-Za-z0-9])\\[\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*\\](?!\\d)/' -%}

{% if notes|length or notesOn or hasMarker %}
{% css %}
.rec-fn{margin:44px 0 0;clear:both}
.rec-fn .rule{height:1px;background:#E2E4E8;margin-bottom:16px}
.rec-fn .lab{font-family:Jost,sans-serif;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472;margin-bottom:13px}
.rec-fn ol{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
.rec-fn li{display:flex;gap:11px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#2C2C2C;margin-bottom:11px}
.rec-fn li .n{flex:0 0 auto;font-family:Jost,sans-serif;font-size:13px;color:#7A5C1B;min-width:1.6em;padding-top:2px}
.rec-fn li:target{background:#FDF7EA}
.rec-fn .back{margin-left:7px;color:#7A5C1B;text-decoration:none;font-size:13px}
.rec-fn .back:hover{text-decoration:underline}
.rec-fn-away{margin:44px 0 0;clear:both;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5B6472}
.rec-fn-away a{color:#7A5C1B}
{#- On paper the arrow back to the text is meaningless. -#}
@media print{.rec-fn .back{display:none}}
{% endcss %}
{% endif %}

{% if notes|length %}
  <section class="rec-fn" id="footnotes">
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <div class="lab">NOTES</div>
    <ol>
      {% for note in notes %}
        <li id="fn-{{ note.n }}">
          <span class="n">{{ note.n }}.</span>
          <span>{{ note.t|nl2br }}<a class="back" href="#fnref-{{ note.n }}" aria-label="Back to the text">&#8617;</a></span>
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>

{% elseif notesOn %}
  <section class="rec-fn-away" id="footnotes">
    The notes for this piece were published separately, on
    <a href="{{ notesOn.url }}">{{ notesOn.title }}</a>.
  </section>

{% elseif hasMarker %}
  <section class="rec-fn-away" id="footnotes">
    The numbered markers in this piece are the author's. The notes they refer to
    are not in the source we hold, so each one says so rather than linking
    to nothing.
  </section>
{% endif %}
